Here's the structured goal model for the multi-robot food delivery system, incorporating the considerations and decompositions:

### Goals Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title                             | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type      | Relation |
|--------|----------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|---------------|----------|
| G1     | Achieve Successful Mission              | Ensure food delivery and dish retrieval are successfully completed. | -                 | Achieve       | -        |
| G1.1   | Achieve Successful Food Delivery      | Deliver food to the inpatient room successfully.                   | -                 | Achieve       | AND      | G1 needs both delivery and retrieval, so AND with G1.2. |
| G1.1.1 | Deliver Food Directly                  | Deliver food directly to the room without assistance.              | -                 | Perform        | OR       | Either direct or assisted delivery can fulfill G1.1. |
| G1.1.2 | Request Assisted Delivery             | Arrange assistance for food delivery if needed.                     | -                 | Perform        | OR       | Alternative to direct delivery. |
| G1.2   | Achieve Successful Dish Retrieval      | Retrieve dirty dishes from the room successfully.                   | -                 | Achieve       | AND      | Required alongside delivery for mission success. |
| G1.2.1 | Request Assisted Dish Retrieval       | Arrange assistance for dish retrieval if needed.                     | -                 | Perform        | OR       | Either unassisted or assisted retrieval can fulfill G1.2. |

### Tasks Table

| Task ID | Task Title                        | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots |
|---------|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------|-------------------|-----------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Room                 | Move to the inpatient's room.                                         | AND       | Inpatient Room    | 1               |
| AT2     | Deliver Food                      | Place food on the room table or hand it over.                        | Sequential | Inpatient Room    | 1               |
| AT3     | Move to Room for Retrieval        | Navigate to the room for dish retrieval.                              | AND       | Inpatient Room    | 1               |
| AT4     | Retrieve Dishes                   | Collect dirty dishes from the room.                                    | Sequential | Inpatient Room    | 1               |
| AT5     | Track Meal Retrieval              | Monitor and record meal retrieval times.                              | AND       | Hospital System   | 1               |
| AT6     | Alert on Wrong Meal Retrieval     | Notify if a wrong meal is retrieved.                                  | AND       | Hospital System   | 1               |
| AT7     | Move to Door                      | Navigate to the room door.                                            | AND       | Inpatient Room    | 1               |
| AT8     | Open Door                         | Open the room door.                                                  | Sequential | Inpatient Room    | 1               |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G1.1, G1.2 [AND]**: Both food delivery and dish retrieval are necessary for mission success.
- **G1.1 -> G1.1.1, G1.1.2 [OR]**: Either direct delivery or requesting assistance can fulfill food delivery.
- **G1.2 -> G1.2.1 [OR]**: Either unassisted or assisted retrieval can fulfill dish retrieval.
- **G1.1.1 -> AT1, AT2 [AND]**: Sequential tasks for navigating to the room and delivering food.
- **G1.2.1 -> AT3, AT4 [AND]**: Sequential tasks for navigating to the room and retrieving dishes.

This model ensures that the system can handle various scenarios, from direct delivery to needing assistance, while efficiently tracking and alerting as necessary.
